<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The respirator's intake, sustained by Ability_AbsorbGas for as long as a draw runs (that
    class's comment has the wiring). The clip is Core's tornado roar (Misc/Tornado/TornadoLoop,
    the Tornado SoundDef's), reused by clipPath; Tornado itself cannot be reused, as its volume,
    range and voice cap are in its def. The roar is quietened, pitched up and shortened into an
    intake:
    - volumeRange 14, a fifth of the tornado's 70: between Core's orbital targeter aiming loop
      (10) and its fire click (18), well under the vent's GasReleasing hiss (35), so the
      respirator never masks the gunfire it is used under.
    - pitchRange 1.3~1.5 makes the weather-sized roar smaller (Unity resamples, so it also runs
      faster); the spread keeps two pilots drawing at once from phasing.
    - distRange 10~30 is GasPack_Deploy's, so the absorb carries as far as the set's other sounds.
    - sustainAttack 0.4 s fades the roar in; SampleSustainer skips the first sample's attack
      unless sustainSkipFirstAttack is false. sustainRelease is left out: it only applies at a
      sample's scheduled end, which a looping sample never reaches at the default
      sustainLoopDurationRange. The tail is sustainFadeoutTime, 0.6 s: Sustainer.End keeps the
      sustainer alive and SampleSustainer fades it over that span. Both are real seconds, so at
      3x speed (a 300-tick draw is about 1.7 s) the roar is still heard.
    - randomStartPoint, as the draw is far shorter than the loop and every cast would otherwise
      play the same opening seconds.
    - maxSimultaneous 2 with PrioritizeNearest: the two nearest drawing pilots are heard.
    tempoAffectedByGameSpeed, muteWhenPaused and canVacuumDampen keep their defaults, as on
    GasReleasing, so a paused draw keeps sounding as the vent's hiss does.
  -->
  <SoundDef>
    <defName>TXWC_AbsorbGasDraw</defName>
    <sustain>true</sustain>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxSimultaneous>2</maxSimultaneous>
    <priorityMode>PrioritizeNearest</priorityMode>
    <sustainFadeoutTime>0.6</sustainFadeoutTime>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip">
            <clipPath>Misc/Tornado/TornadoLoop</clipPath>
          </li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>14~14</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>1.3~1.5</pitchRange>
        <distRange>10~30</distRange>
        <sustainAttack>0.4</sustainAttack>
        <sustainSkipFirstAttack>false</sustainSkipFirstAttack>
        <randomStartPoint>true</randomStartPoint>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>
</Defs>
